{
 "fps": 30,
 "total": 165.833,
 "audio": "none (subtitle-only video, tts_engine none)",
 "sentences": [
  {
   "id": "S01",
   "start": 0.26666666666666666,
   "end": 6.0,
   "text": "Every screen here is a real run, and anything that is not one is labeled.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S02",
   "start": 6.533333333333333,
   "end": 12.8,
   "text": "In 2026 a court found that a quote cited to Cooter and Gell was not in that opinion.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S03",
   "start": 13.133333333333333,
   "end": 19.1,
   "text": "Lookup tools ask whether the case exists. QuoteProof asks whether the quoted words are in it.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S04",
   "start": 19.733333333333334,
   "end": 25.4,
   "text": "Paid tools check quotes too but publish no error rates; here sources are free and rates public.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S05",
   "start": 25.866666666666667,
   "end": 30.066666666666666,
   "text": "Real run: the quote the court rejected, checked against two independent sources.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S06",
   "start": 30.633333333333333,
   "end": 36.9,
   "text": "Both sources report not found, so the verdict is HOLD with a receipt hash anyone can recompute.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S07",
   "start": 37.266666666666666,
   "end": 40.5,
   "text": "Real run: a genuine sentence from Gideon versus Wainwright.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S08",
   "start": 41.03333333333333,
   "end": 46.733333333333334,
   "text": "Both sources find it at a position, so it passes and the receipt records where.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S09",
   "start": 47.166666666666664,
   "end": 51.166666666666664,
   "text": "Now the same sentence with its meaning flipped by three small edits.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S10",
   "start": 51.766666666666666,
   "end": 57.03333333333333,
   "text": "Neither source has it, so the verdict is HOLD and the receipt hash changes.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S11",
   "start": 57.43333333333333,
   "end": 63.1,
   "text": "New in version three: one command extracts every quotation from a brief file and checks each one.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S12",
   "start": 63.666666666666664,
   "end": 70.9,
   "text": "Two invented quotes are held and two genuine ones pass; a lower court cite is not checked, never passed.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S13",
   "start": 71.26666666666667,
   "end": 78.5,
   "text": "Only citation addresses leave the machine, and the tool waits the ten seconds Cornell's robots file asks for.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S14",
   "start": 79.13333333333334,
   "end": 86.9,
   "text": "Id and supra now follow to their case, and when they cannot, the row says why instead of guessing.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S15",
   "start": 87.36666666666666,
   "end": 93.1,
   "text": "The strict default misses the ten percent false alarm target: thirteen point two percent.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S16",
   "start": 93.66666666666667,
   "end": 100.4,
   "text": "Most false alarms are the two sources disagreeing rather than the matching rules, and the miss rate is optimistic.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S17",
   "start": 100.76666666666667,
   "end": 107.43333333333334,
   "text": "Four local processes (not CRE nodes) each read both sources live; three of four must agree and all four do.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S18",
   "start": 107.96666666666667,
   "end": 113.26666666666667,
   "text": "Running the same input at a different clock time gives the identical receipt hash.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S19",
   "start": 113.7,
   "end": 119.96666666666667,
   "text": "The simulator runs this workflow once per node (local): read both sources, agree, then write the report.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S20",
   "start": 120.56666666666666,
   "end": 127.83333333333333,
   "text": "The CRE simulator ran it for real, exit code zero: consensus PASS and a dry run write.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S21",
   "start": 128.23333333333332,
   "end": 133.56666666666666,
   "text": "The altered payload gives HOLD with NOT_IN_OPINION through the same workflow and the same write path.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S22",
   "start": 134.13333333333333,
   "end": 143.13333333333333,
   "text": "The receiver accepts only the forwarder from Chainlink's docs: a real Sepolia transaction (simulator --broadcast, mock forwarder) wrote the verdict; a direct call reverts.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S23",
   "start": 143.46666666666667,
   "end": 152.16666666666666,
   "text": "Opt-in: with --cre-broadcast the same command sends the checked quote into the CRE simulator; its hash matches the local receipt.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S24",
   "start": 152.8,
   "end": 159.16666666666666,
   "text": "Limits first: Supreme Court opinions only, small test sets, and a post hoc policy that is not the headline.",
   "pause_before": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "S25",
   "start": 159.63333333333333,
   "end": 164.63333333333333,
   "text": "QuoteProof checks the words and not only the case, and it states its limits first.",
   "pause_before": 0
  }
 ],
